---
// Tables that span the content column, so several in a row line up as one. The last column holds
// only a status badge and is as wide as one, the name a short one, and what it is the rest.
// Starlight shows a table as a block sized to its content. A cell's width mixing a percentage and
// a length in calc() is read as auto, so the name's width is a plain percentage.
---

<div class="status-tables"><slot /></div>

<style>
  .status-tables :global(table) {
    display: table;
    width: 100%;
    table-layout: fixed;
  }
  .status-tables :global(th:first-child) {
    width: 20%;
  }
  .status-tables :global(th:last-child) {
    width: 7rem;
  }
</style>
